            <ArticleTitle>Elevated left ventricular stiffness by noradrenaline in myocardial ischaemia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>945-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Infusion of noradrenaline (1.0 mug/kg/min body weight, i.v.) brings about an increase of the diastolic wall stiffness in the ischaemic canine heart. Similar effect is not elicitable in the normal heart.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
